{"ok":true,"total":5,"succeeded":5,"failed":0,"concurrency":3,"durationMs":127991,"results":[{"id":"1-sumie-A","ok":true,"path":"/Users/jhuang/Desktop/JH-Projects/risk3d/_claude/themes-zen/1-sumie-A.png","sourcePath":"/Users/jhuang/.codex/generated_images/01a0e8c9-dc2b-7d51-b8b3-fa49661a3731/exec-f469eab7-1cf5-4887-8fb0-3c0b4e4633bc.png","revisedPrompt":"Create exactly one final raster image, wide 16:9 desktop video game screenshot for a fictional game titled \"War Table\". Show the entire board mid-game: a recognizable, geographically coherent stylized world map with the Americas, Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia, subdivided into clear strategy-game territories owned by four players. Ownership colors must use traditional pigments only: vermilion red, indigo blue, ochre gold, and jade green. Apply ownership as restrained translucent pigment washes plus small hanko-style seal stamps in the corresponding player color. Every territory contains exactly one tiny brushed-ink army figure and a clear, small readable numeric troop count.\n\nVisual style: premium Japanese sumi-e ink wash on warm, subtly fibrous rice paper. Continents and borders painted in expressive black brush strokes with soft wet-edge washes, varied ink density, organic imperfect edges, Zen restraint, wabi-sabi elegance. Lots of negative space, calm composition, minimal interface, sophisticated museum-quality art direction. The map remains immediately legible as a world-conquest strategy board inspired by classic territory-control tabletop games, but is wholly original and contains no third-party logos or branded elements.\n\nInclude only one slim, quiet bottom UI bar with delicate brush calligraphy and hairline rules. It must clearly and accurately display the turn track text: \"Place  Attack  Fortify  End turn\". Also include two small understated buttons labeled exactly \"Roll\" and \"Blitz\". Keep all interface text readable, correctly spelled, and sparse. No other panels, menus, overlays, decorative clutter, watermark, signature, or logo. High detail, balanced whole-board composition, polished AAA-quality screenshot, visually serene and playable.","bytes":2846729,"durationMs":68709,"attempts":1,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","modelProvider":"openai","reasoningEffort":"low","threadId":"01a0e8c9-dc2b-7d51-b8b3-fa49661a3731"},{"id":"1-sumie-C","ok":true,"path":"/Users/jhuang/Desktop/JH-Projects/risk3d/_claude/themes-zen/1-sumie-C.png","sourcePath":"/Users/jhuang/.codex/generated_images/01a0e8c9-dbdd-7ea2-99cf-0c0e4b633589/exec-9f272cff-b214-465c-bdc7-7d707bb4af28.png","revisedPrompt":"Create exactly one final raster image: a tall portrait 9:19.5 smartphone video-game screenshot for a restrained, elegant world-conquest strategy board game titled “War Table,” in the spirit of classic territory-conquest board games. The game board fills nearly the entire screen and shows a recognizable stylized world map with the Americas, Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia, divided into distinct readable territories. Four players own territories, indicated only by translucent traditional pigment washes—vermilion red, indigo blue, ochre gold, and jade green—and by small matching hanko-style seal stamps. Each territory contains exactly one tiny brushed-ink army figure and a clear small numeric troop count. Visual style: premium Japanese sumi-e ink wash on warm, subtly fibrous rice paper; continents and borders painted with expressive black brush strokes, varied dry-brush texture, soft wet-edge washes, restrained imperfections, Zen negative space, wabi-sabi elegance. Minimal calm UI: four tiny player color markers aligned at the top; at the bottom, a delicate hairline-rule bar with readable brush-calligraphy labels “Place   Attack   Fortify   End” and one distinct but restrained “Blitz” button. Keep all text correctly spelled and legible. Very little chrome, no extra panels, no clutter. High detail, beautiful, polished commercial game screenshot, balanced hierarchy, readable map and troop numbers, no watermark, no device frame, no hands, no perspective mockup—only the flat full-screen game screenshot.","bytes":3039290,"durationMs":52266,"attempts":1,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","modelProvider":"openai","reasoningEffort":"low","threadId":"01a0e8c9-dbdd-7ea2-99cf-0c0e4b633589"},{"id":"2-shanshui-A","ok":true,"path":"/Users/jhuang/Desktop/JH-Projects/risk3d/_claude/themes-zen/2-shanshui-A.png","sourcePath":"/Users/jhuang/.codex/generated_images/01a0e8c9-dbbe-7790-b073-b61b955f3918/exec-f580a239-e4bd-49fd-a907-7761aa21ac65.png","revisedPrompt":"Use case: ui-mockup\nAsset type: final raster video game screenshot, wide 16:9 desktop view\nPrimary request: Create a polished screenshot of a restrained, elegant world-conquest strategy board game titled “War Table,” in the spirit of classic Risk. Show the entire game board mid-game.\nScene/backdrop: A recognizable stylized world map with the Americas, Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia, divided into readable territories. The continents rise as misty mountain islands from a sea of drifting mist and delicate fine wave linework.\nSubject: Four players own territories in traditional pigment colors: vermilion red, indigo blue, ochre gold, and jade green. Every territory contains exactly one small, finely drawn army figure with a pennant in its owning player color and a clear, small integer number beside or on its base.\nStyle/medium: Chinese shan shui blue-green landscape painting, qinglü aesthetic inspired by Song dynasty silk scrolls; mineral blue-green and ochre pigments, delicate gongbi outlines, atmospheric layered mountains, subtle aged silk texture. Premium game art, high detail, graceful and calm.\nComposition/framing: Wide landscape 16:9, slightly elevated top-down board view, whole world visible and geographically recognizable, generous negative space and mist, balanced visual hierarchy, map remains readable as a strategy board.\nUI: Very little UI. Include only one slim, quiet bottom bar styled like a mounted scroll with a thin brocade border. Within it, show the turn track text exactly: “Place  Attack  Fortify  End turn”. Include two small buttons labeled exactly “Roll” and “Blitz”. No other panels, cards, menus, counters, tooltips, logos, or overlays.\nTypography/text: Render the title “War Table” subtly and elegantly. All requested UI labels must be crisp and readable; army numbers must be small but legible.\nColor palette: Mineral blue-green, jade, muted indigo, vermilion accents, ochre gold, warm silk ivory, restrained saturation.\nMood: Contemplative, strategic, refined, museum-quality, spacious.\nConstraints: Exactly four player colors; each territory has one army piece and one clear number; continents and territorial divisions are recognizable; whole board visible; bottom UI does not obscure the map; no watermark.\nAvoid: busy modern HUD, neon colors, glossy 3D plastic, photorealism, excessive UI, illegible map labels, clutter, duplicated buttons, misspelled text, extra text, watermark.","bytes":3083156,"durationMs":70881,"attempts":1,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","modelProvider":"openai","reasoningEffort":"low","threadId":"01a0e8c9-dbbe-7790-b073-b61b955f3918"},{"id":"2-shanshui-C","ok":true,"path":"/Users/jhuang/Desktop/JH-Projects/risk3d/_claude/themes-zen/2-shanshui-C.png","sourcePath":"/Users/jhuang/.codex/generated_images/01a0e8ca-a7a0-7150-89e3-52b9bb2256c4/exec-1d7fed82-fd79-45d4-88a5-e4cae14f6d04.png","revisedPrompt":"Create exactly one final raster image: a tall portrait 9:19.5 smartphone video-game screenshot for a fictional board game titled “War Table.” The board fills almost the entire screen and depicts a recognizable, geographically coherent stylized world map with the Americas, Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia, divided into clear conquest-game territories owned by four players. Use four traditional pigment faction colors consistently: vermilion red, indigo blue, ochre gold, and jade green. Every territory contains exactly one small, finely drawn army figure with a pennant matching its owner and a clear small Arabic numeral that remains readable at phone-screen scale.\n\nArt direction: restrained, elegant Chinese shan shui blue-green landscape painting (qinglü, Song-dynasty-inspired), with continents rising like misty mountain islands from a sea of drifting mist and delicate fine wave linework; mineral blue-green and ochre palette, delicate gongbi outlines, subtle silk-scroll texture, premium museum-quality detail. Preserve geographic recognizability and gameplay readability despite the painterly style. Calm composition, generous negative space, sparse UI, refined and beautiful.\n\nUI: four tiny player markers aligned discreetly at the top in vermilion, indigo, ochre, and jade. A minimal mounted-scroll-style bottom bar with a thin brocade border. The bottom bar must show these legible labels in this exact order: “Place   Attack   Fortify   End”. Include one distinct but restrained button labeled exactly “Blitz”. No other prominent UI. No watermark, no logo, no extraneous text, no modern neon effects, no photorealistic phone hardware or hand—show the screenshot itself edge-to-edge.","bytes":3264870,"durationMs":54881,"attempts":1,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","modelProvider":"openai","reasoningEffort":"low","threadId":"01a0e8ca-a7a0-7150-89e3-52b9bb2256c4"},{"id":"3-karesansui-A","ok":true,"path":"/Users/jhuang/Desktop/JH-Projects/risk3d/_claude/themes-zen/3-karesansui-A.png","sourcePath":"/Users/jhuang/.codex/generated_images/01a0e8ca-e791-7e00-9832-4b31aee075dd/exec-c010b153-7518-4dec-adfc-2030d4e8d3b8.png","revisedPrompt":"Create exactly one final raster image.\n\nA premium video game screenshot for a restrained, elegant world-conquest strategy board game titled “War Table,” inspired by the broad visual language of classic territory-conquest board games but with an original board and interface. Wide 16:9 desktop view, orthographic/top-down with slight dimensionality, showing the entire board mid-game.\n\nThe board is a recognizable stylized world map with the Americas, Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia, divided into clearly readable territories. Four players own territories using traditional pigment colors: vermilion red, indigo blue, ochre gold, and jade green. Every territory contains exactly one small carved wooden army token shaped like a shogi piece, bearing a crisp, clearly legible small integer. Ownership colors should be restrained accents or washes integrated naturally into the moss-and-stone land, while remaining easy to distinguish.\n\nArt direction: Japanese karesansui zen rock garden viewed from above. The ocean is finely raked white gravel; elegant concentric ripple lines flow around every continent and island. Continents are moss and weathered stone islands. Territory borders are thin bamboo-like lines. Soft morning light creates delicate, realistic shadows. High material detail, calm composition, generous negative space, extreme restraint, museum-quality craftsmanship.\n\nVery little UI. One slim, quiet stone-grey bar along the bottom only. In thin, refined sans-serif typography, include the turn track exactly as: “Place   Attack   Fortify   End turn”. Include two small understated buttons labeled exactly “Roll” and “Blitz”. No other panels, popups, legends, badges, or clutter. The game title “War Table” may appear very subtly at the upper left, small and elegant.\n\nPrioritize an immediately recognizable whole-world board, clear territory divisions, readable token numbers, accurate requested labels, and a believable polished game screenshot. No watermark, no logos, no excessive ornament, no fantasy scenery, no photoreal human hands, no dice in motion, no crowded interface.","bytes":3497654,"durationMs":58964,"attempts":1,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","modelProvider":"openai","reasoningEffort":"low","threadId":"01a0e8ca-e791-7e00-9832-4b31aee075dd"}]}
